1
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:43,440
Yiran!

2
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:48,400
Yiran!

3
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,120
Come help me peel some garlic.

4
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:54,880
What are you doing?

5
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,960
You've been sitting there forever.

6
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,520
You can't even peel garlic.

7
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,520
You obviously eat takeout every day.

8
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:33,480
Forget it.

9
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,600
Here, give it to me.

10
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,960
Go beat two eggs for me.

11
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:05,320
Like a bull

12
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:08,560
in a china shop.

13
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,760
My hand just slipped, okay?

14
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,480
You talk too much.

15
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:24,680
I suddenly remember when I first got married.

16
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,720
When I went into the kitchen, I

17
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,360
broke an egg too.

18
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:31,200
Your Pops said I was

19
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,760
like a bull

20
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:35,640
in a china shop.

21
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:44,760
Are you making chicken soup?

22
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,040
You've got a sharp nose.

23
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:49,520
Is it ready yet?

24
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:51,040
I'm hungry.

25
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,160
I'll go check.

26
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:28,920
Here.

27
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,640
How's the seasoning?

28
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:47,960
Not salty.

29
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:53,880
Granny Xiufang used to make chicken soup for us too.

30
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,520
It was so salty Chen Baixi and I almost threw up.

31
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:59,760
When people get older,

32
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,880
their sense of taste fades.

33
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,360
But even chicken soup like that,

34
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:14,520
we'll never get to have it again.

35
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,800
Stop acting all deep with me.

36
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,760
Don't cry.

37
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,520
From now on,

38
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,480
whenever you drink chicken soup,

39
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:32,000
won't you think of Granny Xiufang?

40
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,680
Just like me.

41
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,440
Whenever I go into the kitchen,

42
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:36,720
I think of your Pops.

43
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,480
Even though some people are gone,

44
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:45,360
as long as we, the living, remember them, that's enough.

45
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:16,440
The clothes are in the back room.

46
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:34,440
Xiwa.

47
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,800
Grandma found you!

48
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,000
Is it tasty?

49
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,880
It is.

50
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,200
Grandma, have some too.

51
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,360
Grandma, when I grow up,

52
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:10,760
I'll buy you lots of brown sugar glutinous rice cakes.

53
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:12,600
Okay.

54
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,800
My Xiwa is so sweet.

55
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:16,720
Grandma will be waiting.

56
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:22,400
Grandma doesn't know

57
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,280
how tall you've grown.

58
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:30,720
Grandma doesn't know

59
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:33,600
if she'd still recognize you.

60
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,000
Have you seen my boy?

61
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,000
My boy!

62
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,080
My boy!

63
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,080
Xiwa!

64
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,320
Xiwa!

65
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,160
Xiwa!

66
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,200
Come home.

67
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,200
It's been twenty years.

68
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:55,960
Grandma

69
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,120
is taking my Xiwa home.

70
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,360
Xiwa!

71
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:04,160
Come home.

72
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,240
Come home.

73
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,880
Before Granny passed away,

74
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:19,680
what did she say to you?

75
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:24,840
Granny...

76
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:29,400
Granny has something to tell you.

77
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,280
Tell me, Granny.

78
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,840
I know

79
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,080
that you

80
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:39,160
aren't my Xiwa.

81
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:45,960
But you're my good grandson.

82
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:49,080
I also know

83
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:51,760
you have something

84
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:53,160
on your mind.

85
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:56,880
Let Granny tell you this.

86
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:58,800
Look forward,

87
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:02,480
don't look back.

88
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:09,840
Don't look back.

89
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,600
She told me

90
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,240
that finding me

91
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:29,440
and having me by her side

92
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,120
made her very happy.

93
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,040
Pops.

94
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:09,080
Are you really okay with my brother doing this?

95
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:11,720
Sincerity matters more than formality.

96
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,800
He's the best person for it.

97
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:57,040
A stick of incense opens the path to the netherworld

98
00:12:57,560 --> 00:13:03,720
Beloved parent, depart without worldly cares

99
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:09,840
May light illuminate the Three Paths

100
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,320
The mighty wind sweeps away impurities,

101
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,240
the divine light guards the path.

102
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:52,600
Grandma,

103
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:54,080
I've opened the path for you.

104
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:18,240
The silver bridge crosses worldly suffering,

105
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,920
the golden bridge leads to the Jade Capital.

106
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:26,080
The gentle soul steps firmly on the lotus,

107
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:30,560
To wander freely in peace forevermore.

108
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:33,160
Crossing the bridge!

109
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:38,640
Crossing the bridge!

110
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:41,760
Crossing the bridge!

111
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,800
Crossing the bridge!

112
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:50,040
Stepping on lotus flowers, rising ever higher.

113
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:55,440
The Gold Bridge leads to the highest heavens.

114
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:58,120
Granny,

115
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,840
You are deeply blessed.

116
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:05,720
Step firmly on the Gold Bridge and don't look back.

117
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:21,160
Crossing the bridge!

118
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:25,520
Crossing the bridge!

119
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:29,640
Crossing the bridge!

120
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:32,880
Crossing the bridge!

121
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:53,400
Grandma.

122
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,600
There's light on the bridge.

123
00:15:59,240 --> 00:16:00,400
Take your time.

124
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:02,480
Cross safely.

125
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,480
Once you cross the bridge,

126
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,960
you'll see Xizi.

127
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:29,400
These sugar glutinous rice cakes,

128
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:30,880
take them with you.

129
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:34,320
Passing on won't be so bitter.

130
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,800
You won't have to worry about this world's

131
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:39,960
trivial matters anymore.

132
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,760
Please pay your respects.

133
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,360
First bow.

134
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:09,040
Second bow.

135
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:11,680
Third bow.

136
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,120
Family, return the bow.

137
00:17:59,320 --> 00:17:59,960
Here.

138
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:03,120
Here.

139
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:03,760
Take this.

140
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:07,360
Here.

141
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:08,680
Here you go.

142
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,800
Daxi.

143
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:15,480
I'm leaving.

144
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:17,360
Stay strong.

145
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,240
Kid.

146
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,560
Look forward.

147
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,680
Stop spacing out.

148
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:23,840
What are you looking at?

149
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,480
Nothing.

150
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:30,160
Just saw some familiar faces.

151
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:33,600
Where?

152
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,440
They already left.

153
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:08,680
Boss Chen,

154
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:10,720
Eating all by yourself?

155
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:14,920
When you get old,

156
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:16,720
nobody wants you around.

157
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:19,880
I enjoy eating alone. It's quite nice.

158
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:23,920
Boss, two plates of beef slices.

159
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:24,760
Alright.

160
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:31,560
Dad.

161
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:33,280
I have something to tell you.

162
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,520
I know what you're gonna say.

163
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:41,840
Wait a second.

164
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:45,320
Let me speak first.

165
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:49,920
What happened with Granny Xiufang today...

166
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:54,320
Even though you broke the rules,

167
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:58,080
it was the reasonable thing to do.

168
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:01,680
The funeral industry

169
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:03,960
isn't a glamorous business.

170
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:07,560
People see it as taboo.

171
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:13,800
But it's our family's lifeblood.

172
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,920
What's the old saying?

173
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:22,560
It runs

174
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,560
in the family.

175
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:31,960
So, I want my son to carry it on,

176
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:35,160
to do our ancestors proud.

177
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:38,920
Dad...

178
00:22:38,920 --> 00:22:40,360
I know.

179
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:42,800
Over this very thing,

180
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:46,200
we've been at odds for years.

181
00:22:47,960 --> 00:22:50,080
I also know

182
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:52,960
you have a dream in your heart.

183
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:55,600
If you want to leave now,

184
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:56,960
I won't stop you.

185
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:59,120
After all,

186
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,200
people have to live for themselves.

187
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:10,520
Dad, what I actually wanted to say is...

188
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,840
I don't want to leave.

189
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:13,920
Not leaving?

190
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:18,240
What did you say?

191
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:22,640
Dad, what's with that look?

192
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:24,520
I said I'm not leaving, is that a problem?

193
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:30,200
You said you could only realize your dream in Beijing.

194
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:33,440
When I was in Beijing,

195
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:36,040
I took the subway every day.

196
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:37,880
Whenever I got on,

197
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:39,160
have you seen a can of sardines?

198
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:41,040
I was squeezed like a can of sardines.

199
00:23:41,040 --> 00:23:42,640
Stinky and ugly.

200
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:44,520
Sometimes there wasn't even room to stand.

201
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:45,760
It was incredibly crowded.

202
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:47,360
From one audition

203
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:49,280
to another,

204
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,760
I even had to work odd jobs at night.

205
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:52,200
Then I had to catch the last train home.

206
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,440
It made me feel like

207
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:55,480
a spinning top that never stops.

208
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,320
Going round and round,

209
00:23:57,320 --> 00:23:59,520
I didn't even know who I was anymore.

210
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:04,000
Over all these years,

211
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:07,560
the only time I gave a stellar performance

212
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:09,320
was wearing sackcloth on set for a funeral.

213
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:12,320
Crying and wailing,

214
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:13,160
like there was no tomorrow.

215
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:14,400
"Oh, Dad!"

216
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:17,320
Everyone applauded, calling me a filial son.

217
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:18,440
This is how I acted.

218
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:20,720
"Oh, Dad!

219
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:22,680
Why did you die so tragically?"

220
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:26,200
Tears just kept streaming down my face.

221
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:31,000
Are you cursing me to die, boy?

222
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:34,200
I saw it a lot with you when I was a kid.

223
00:24:40,760 --> 00:24:43,720
Dad, I know

224
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:45,360
Paradise Funeral Home is your life's work,

225
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:47,440
and the root of our family.

226
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:50,440
I want to stay and help you.

227
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:52,720
Help me?

228
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:58,320
Mainly, I've felt pretty fulfilled lately.

229
00:24:58,320 --> 00:24:59,880
Pretty grounded, too.

230
00:24:59,880 --> 00:25:02,080
Sunrise brings hope,

231
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:03,360
sunset brings reflection.

232
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:09,800
I feel like I'm no longer drifting.

233
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:21,200
You son of a bitch.

234
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:25,880
Did you have too much to drink?

235
00:25:26,080 --> 00:25:28,360
I... I haven't even started drinking yet.

236
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:42,800
Dad.

237
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,000
Thank you.

238
00:25:59,520 --> 00:26:00,800
Kid,

239
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:04,680
our funeral business,

240
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:07,160
to put it bluntly,

241
00:26:07,160 --> 00:26:09,560
comes down to two things.

242
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:11,880
The left hand

243
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:16,480
is helping the departed pass on in peace.

244
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,160
The right hand

245
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:22,920
is giving the living a place to cry.

246
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:29,040
In other words, this job of ours

247
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:31,560
is half in the earth,

248
00:26:32,120 --> 00:26:34,840
and half

249
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:36,920
in the heart.

250
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,920
Once you take this step,

251
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:50,320
there's no turning back.

252
00:26:52,160 --> 00:26:53,120
Of course,

253
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:56,480
if you regret it,

254
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,640
it's not too late.

255
00:27:00,080 --> 00:27:00,880
I don't regret it.

256
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:10,880
No regrets.

257
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:16,760
Then eat up.

258
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,000
Eat.

259
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:21,520
The pot's boiling. Add some food.

260
00:27:23,080 --> 00:27:23,880
Thanks.

261
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,360
In this line of work,

262
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:40,760
it's about respecting heaven, earth, others, and yourself.

263
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:42,560
Chen Baixi,

264
00:27:42,560 --> 00:27:43,960
have you thought this through?

265
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:46,080
I have.

266
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:47,280
Good.

267
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:55,600
Founding Master above,

268
00:27:55,600 --> 00:28:00,080
today, Chen Jianguo asks heaven, earth, and Founding Master,

269
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:03,200
if my son, Chen Baixi,

270
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:06,120
can inherit my mantle.

271
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:27,120
Ask again.

272
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:48,960
If the Founding Master truly lets him pass on the teachings,

273
00:28:48,960 --> 00:28:51,960
please grant the divination blocks again.

274
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:06,120
The Founding Master

275
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:07,560
has agreed.

276
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:10,440
Kneel down.

277
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:31,040
This profession isn't just the final stop for the dead,

278
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:34,960
it's also a comfort for the living.

279
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:37,920
Remember.

280
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:42,680
Kindness first, dedication foremost.

281
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:47,120
Hold compassion in your heart, act with measure.

282
00:29:47,720 --> 00:29:49,360
Comfort the hearts of the living,

283
00:29:49,360 --> 00:29:53,360
rest the souls of the departed.

284
00:30:01,120 --> 00:30:02,760
I will remember your teachings.

285
00:30:33,080 --> 00:30:34,680
Are you sure you don't regret staying?

286
00:30:36,120 --> 00:30:37,000
No regrets.

287
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:38,720
Why?

288
00:30:40,120 --> 00:30:41,000
Same as you.

289
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:43,440
Maybe the evening breeze here,

290
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:44,920
more than the dreams in Beijing,

291
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:46,840
understands my worth better.

292
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:48,480
You copycat, Chen Baixi.

293
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:51,680
Oh, right.

294
00:30:52,840 --> 00:30:53,720
This is for you.

295
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:56,200
For me?

296
00:30:57,280 --> 00:30:59,920
You were going back to Shanghai before,

297
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:01,080
so I got a gift for you.

298
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:02,240
But then you didn't leave,

299
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:04,360
so I just

300
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:05,320
never gave it to you.

301
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:07,320
What is it?

302
00:31:08,360 --> 00:31:09,800
A cheap little trinket.

303
00:31:09,800 --> 00:31:10,800
It's cheap?

304
00:31:10,800 --> 00:31:11,960
Then I don't want it.

305
00:31:12,200 --> 00:31:12,760
No, wait.

306
00:31:12,760 --> 00:31:13,600
It's cheap,

307
00:31:13,920 --> 00:31:15,800
it's cheap, but it's...

308
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:16,680
it's very meaningful.

309
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:21,640
I'm opening it.

310
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:26,280
Yiran Star.

311
00:31:27,920 --> 00:31:29,520
I went online and bought you

312
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:31,520
the naming rights to a star.

313
00:31:31,520 --> 00:31:32,480
This is the certificate.

314
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:36,680
From now on, there's a star in the sky

315
00:31:36,680 --> 00:31:37,880
that belongs to you.

316
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:41,520
Even though you can't see or touch it,

317
00:31:41,680 --> 00:31:44,200
it's right there.

318
00:31:45,120 --> 00:31:46,320
It'll always be there.

319
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:06,360
Thanks.

320
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:08,640
I really like it.

321
00:32:12,080 --> 00:32:12,840
I'll put it away.

322
00:33:03,080 --> 00:33:05,360
Where should it go?

323
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:07,080
White or black?

324
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:08,440
White.

325
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:09,240
Right.

326
00:33:09,240 --> 00:33:10,960
We'll put it here.

327
00:33:15,120 --> 00:33:16,000
Done.

328
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,120
Excellent.

329
00:33:17,120 --> 00:33:20,920
Today's a good day.

330
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:23,720
You're in a good mood today.

331
00:33:23,720 --> 00:33:24,760
You have no idea.

332
00:33:25,160 --> 00:33:26,880
That son of a bitch of mine...

333
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:28,280
He's finally settled down.

334
00:33:28,280 --> 00:33:29,920
He's decided to take over the business.

335
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:30,440
Really?

336
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:33,000
That's a huge weight off my mind.

337
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:35,120
Mom.

338
00:33:35,120 --> 00:33:37,840
Uncle A Min said he'd come play today.

339
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:39,960
It's been so long, and he's not here.

340
00:33:41,040 --> 00:33:41,800
A Min?

341
00:33:42,440 --> 00:33:44,760
You mean our Blockhead?

342
00:33:45,800 --> 00:33:46,680
Last time,

343
00:33:46,680 --> 00:33:48,840
Yiran sent him to learn from me.

344
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:51,920
Then he and Yangyang became friends.

345
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:54,040
A Min...

346
00:33:54,040 --> 00:33:56,600
He's just bad with people.

347
00:33:58,520 --> 00:33:59,680
A Min.

348
00:34:02,200 --> 00:34:04,040
I... I just got here.

349
00:34:04,040 --> 00:34:05,680
Then why didn't you go in?

350
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:06,400
Okay.

351
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,320
Jianguo, you're here too.

352
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:11,040
Speak of the devil.

353
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:13,880
A Min, you...

354
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:16,440
Yangyang, I just wrote a new poem.

355
00:34:16,440 --> 00:34:17,680
Come help me take a look.

356
00:34:18,160 --> 00:34:18,960
Brother Chen.

357
00:34:19,440 --> 00:34:20,920
You're getting a haircut here too?

358
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:24,720
Everyone's studying hard here, Juanzi.

359
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:26,640
Sorry.

360
00:34:26,640 --> 00:34:28,040
I... I...

361
00:34:28,600 --> 00:34:29,480
I forgot my money.

362
00:34:30,800 --> 00:34:32,320
I'll get it right now.

363
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:34,280
I'll just pay for you.

364
00:34:34,760 --> 00:34:36,280
I'd feel bad about that.

365
00:34:36,280 --> 00:34:37,720
What's there to feel bad about?

366
00:34:38,040 --> 00:34:39,800
We'll be family anyway.

367
00:34:41,840 --> 00:34:42,680
Family?

368
00:34:47,520 --> 00:34:48,600
I'm not...

369
00:34:49,040 --> 00:34:49,840
You old man.

370
00:34:52,520 --> 00:34:55,200
You should care about your son's marriage.

371
00:34:57,880 --> 00:34:59,200
Do you get it?

372
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:01,240
You...

373
00:35:02,680 --> 00:35:04,400
Okay, I get it.

374
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:05,800
Do you really get it?

375
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:07,200
I think I get it.

376
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:07,800
I get it.

377
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:11,880
Do you get it or not?

378
00:35:12,840 --> 00:35:13,640
Juanzi.

379
00:35:14,560 --> 00:35:15,680
That was scary.

380
00:35:15,680 --> 00:35:17,880
Chen Baixi is just like his old man.

381
00:35:17,880 --> 00:35:19,240
His reactions are so slow.

382
00:35:19,240 --> 00:35:21,160
I seriously can't with him.

383
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,080
Juanzi.

384
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:25,840
I need you to do me a favor.

385
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:26,840
What is it?

386
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:28,720
I found a guy.

387
00:35:28,720 --> 00:35:31,320
He's the classiest guy around here.

388
00:35:31,320 --> 00:35:33,360
You two would be a perfect match.

389
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:37,480
Go on a blind date for me.

390
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:39,720
I'm not in the mood.

391
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:42,680
You're in your prime right now.

392
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:44,160
You're so beautiful.

393
00:35:44,160 --> 00:35:45,080
And your career is going well.

394
00:35:45,080 --> 00:35:46,480
Look, your hair is pretty.

395
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:47,160
Your ears are pretty.

396
00:35:47,160 --> 00:35:47,760
Your earrings are pretty.

397
00:35:47,760 --> 00:35:48,320
Your eyes are pretty.

398
00:35:48,320 --> 00:35:49,000
Your eyebrows are pretty too.

399
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:49,520
Your mouth is pretty too.

400
00:35:49,520 --> 00:35:50,400
Everything about you is pretty.

401
00:35:50,640 --> 00:35:52,800
If you don't enjoy your youth now,

402
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:53,760
when will you?

403
00:35:53,760 --> 00:35:55,040
Don't you think so?

404
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:56,520
Then it's decided.

405
00:35:57,080 --> 00:36:01,240
Saturday, 5 p.m., at Magpie Bridge Tea Restaurant.

406
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:02,560
You definitely won't regret it.

407
00:36:02,560 --> 00:36:03,600
It's settled.

408
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:04,600
Don't say another word.

409
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:05,120
I'm leaving.

410
00:36:05,120 --> 00:36:05,960
That's that, okay?

411
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,040
No, wait.

412
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:07,960
Sister Lan.

413
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:09,920
Sweetie, what's up?

414
00:36:11,240 --> 00:36:13,160
You haven't paid yet.

415
00:36:14,640 --> 00:36:15,960
How much is it?

416
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:18,120
Just a cut is 20.

417
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:20,240
20.

418
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:21,720
Paid. See?

419
00:36:23,520 --> 00:36:24,600
Got it.

420
00:36:30,840 --> 00:36:32,080
Bro.

421
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:36,520
I heard Fan Shiqi gave you a present.

422
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:40,600
Baixi,

423
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:47,200
what brings you here?

424
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:48,720
While I was editing the documentary,

425
00:36:48,720 --> 00:36:50,520
I also cut some clips of Granny Xiufang.

426
00:36:50,960 --> 00:36:52,360
You can keep them as a memento.

427
00:36:57,880 --> 00:36:58,680
Thank you.

428
00:37:02,920 --> 00:37:03,920
Is there anything else?

429
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:08,640
Last time,

430
00:37:08,640 --> 00:37:10,600
I said I liked you.

431
00:37:11,440 --> 00:37:12,960
I just wanted to ask you again,

432
00:37:14,320 --> 00:37:17,400
is there still a chance for us?

433
00:37:22,400 --> 00:37:24,680
What do you think they're whispering about?

434
00:37:26,720 --> 00:37:27,680
If you keep acting like this,

435
00:37:27,680 --> 00:37:30,400
my brother is really gonna be stolen by Miss Fan.

436
00:37:31,440 --> 00:37:32,960
What do you mean, stolen?

437
00:37:33,520 --> 00:37:34,880
Your brother is a person.

438
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:36,080
He has a mind of his own.

439
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:37,640
Whoever he wants to be with

440
00:37:37,640 --> 00:37:39,200
is completely up to him.

441
00:37:41,840 --> 00:37:43,040
Why do I feel like the air

442
00:37:43,040 --> 00:37:45,280
is thick with jealousy?

443
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:47,120
Someone's feeling sour!

444
00:38:05,320 --> 00:38:06,160
Don't talk nonsense.

445
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:09,080
She just gave me some videos of Granny Xiufang.

446
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:13,680
I thought she was confessing her love to you.

447
00:38:14,320 --> 00:38:15,200
Right, Yiran?

448
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:20,720
Chen Xiaofang, why are you such a gossip?

449
00:38:21,960 --> 00:38:24,080
If you have time to mind other people's business,

450
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:25,840
you'd better mind your own first.

451
00:38:29,040 --> 00:38:30,080
Not him again.

452
00:38:30,360 --> 00:38:32,000
Bro, hurry up and kick him out.

453
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:32,920
I don't want to see him.

454
00:38:34,320 --> 00:38:36,280
I heard from Wu Huilian

455
00:38:36,400 --> 00:38:38,960
that Zhou Fang is left with nothing now.

456
00:38:39,320 --> 00:38:41,960
His dad supposedly took back his car and house.

457
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:44,760
He's completely penniless now,

458
00:38:44,760 --> 00:38:45,880
fending for himself.

459
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:48,440
He even texted me yesterday to borrow money.

460
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:51,320
Xiaofang, aren't you gonna do anything?

461
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:53,640
Who knows if he's pretending to be pitiful to trick me?

462
00:38:53,640 --> 00:38:55,600
Just hear what he has to say first.

463
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:07,680
Go on, go on.

464
00:39:12,520 --> 00:39:13,280
Zhou Fang.

465
00:39:14,280 --> 00:39:15,640
I heard you got kicked out of the house.

466
00:39:19,640 --> 00:39:20,360
Xiaofang.

467
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:21,840
I chose to leave.

468
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:23,680
Young Master Zhou,

469
00:39:24,560 --> 00:39:26,320
are you really willing to give up the silver spoon?

470
00:39:26,680 --> 00:39:27,480
For you,

471
00:39:28,760 --> 00:39:30,480
I'm willing to give up anything.

472
00:39:31,600 --> 00:39:33,360
Save the high-sounding nonsense.

473
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:34,680
Chen Xiaofang.

474
00:39:37,720 --> 00:39:39,120
I, Zhou Fang, swear.

475
00:39:40,640 --> 00:39:42,240
Even without my family's help,

476
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:45,600
I can make something of myself.

477
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:50,560
What's he saying?

478
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:52,560
He made a vow,

479
00:39:52,560 --> 00:39:53,960
and then he raised his hand.

480
00:39:56,560 --> 00:39:57,960
Don't just be passionate for a couple of days

481
00:39:58,600 --> 00:40:00,160
and then go back to being daddy's little boy.

482
00:40:01,520 --> 00:40:03,160
I admit I was a jerk before,

483
00:40:05,760 --> 00:40:06,960
but I'm serious now.

484
00:40:09,560 --> 00:40:11,320
I'm not a very patient person.

485
00:40:11,760 --> 00:40:12,720
I can't wait too long.

486
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:14,600
I won't make you wait too long.

487
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:16,080
I'm going back to work hard right now.

488
00:40:42,400 --> 00:40:44,080
Oh my god!

489
00:40:44,080 --> 00:40:45,400
Young Boss Zhou.

490
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:46,800
Are you trying to murder me?

491
00:40:47,160 --> 00:40:48,120
You scared me to death.

492
00:40:48,120 --> 00:40:50,560
I just got a bit excited seeing you.

493
00:40:51,400 --> 00:40:52,880
I just sold my sports car,

494
00:40:52,880 --> 00:40:54,480
and just learned how to ride a bike.

495
00:40:54,480 --> 00:40:56,200
Thought I'd use it to get some exercise.

496
00:40:56,200 --> 00:40:56,960
Oh, really?

497
00:40:57,160 --> 00:40:58,800
This bike is pretty nice.

498
00:41:01,600 --> 00:41:02,920
The seat's not very comfortable.

499
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:05,680
How's yours?

500
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:06,920
Making yourself at home.

501
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:10,720
If I'd known being shameless was this useful,

502
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,320
I would've ditched my pride long ago.

503
00:41:14,320 --> 00:41:17,720
What's the point of saving face anyway?

504
00:41:17,720 --> 00:41:19,920
If saving face were actually useful,

505
00:41:20,600 --> 00:41:22,520
a lot of things would never get done.

506
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:24,640
I'm just keeping Auntie Huilan's words

507
00:41:24,640 --> 00:41:25,680
firmly in mind.

508
00:41:25,680 --> 00:41:26,680
How did it go again?

509
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:30,160
She said, the thickness of your wallet determines the height of your love.

510
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:31,200
It's just that...

511
00:41:31,200 --> 00:41:33,840
I've almost spent all the money from my sports car.

512
00:41:34,960 --> 00:41:35,760
No worries.

513
00:41:36,240 --> 00:41:37,400
Yiran said it herself.

514
00:41:38,080 --> 00:41:39,360
When doing things,

515
00:41:39,480 --> 00:41:40,800
you need to focus.

516
00:41:41,560 --> 00:41:43,600
Addition is human nature,

517
00:41:43,880 --> 00:41:46,160
subtraction is wisdom.

518
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:50,160
I think our Joy Bells

519
00:41:50,160 --> 00:41:52,280
really needs a major reform.

520
00:41:53,200 --> 00:41:55,800
Auntie Huilan, what brilliant idea do you have now?

521
00:41:59,080 --> 00:41:59,880
Let's go.

522
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:02,120
Let's go back and hold a reform meeting.

523
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:03,560
I'll tell you all about it.

524
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:06,160
Our slogan is,

525
00:42:06,160 --> 00:42:08,680
Joyful and harmonious,

526
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:10,720
marry with Xidongdong.

527
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:11,880
Sit down.

528
00:42:12,680 --> 00:42:14,160
Old Wu, you're up.

529
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:16,480
Boss, have a seat.

530
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:22,440
I'll begin now.

531
00:42:23,440 --> 00:42:25,760
I made this presentation.

532
00:42:25,760 --> 00:42:28,320
It's called Spicy Love.

533
00:42:28,320 --> 00:42:30,440
We've all had hot pot, right?

534
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:34,000
You know it's divided into spicy and clear broth.

535
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:35,480
Why is it divided like that?

536
00:42:35,480 --> 00:42:37,600
Because everyone's taste is different.

537
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:39,360
Well, people are the same way.

538
00:42:39,360 --> 00:42:41,480
Divided into I-person (introvert) and E-person (extrovert).

539
00:42:41,840 --> 00:42:42,600
So, we

540
00:42:42,600 --> 00:42:45,520
need to separate these two types of people into different groups.

541
00:42:47,200 --> 00:42:48,400
Let's talk about the I-person (introvert) first.

542
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:52,240
An I-person (introvert) needs to wear a mask

543
00:42:52,480 --> 00:42:53,840
for soul-level socializing.

544
00:42:53,840 --> 00:42:54,920
They can't see your face,

545
00:42:55,200 --> 00:42:57,080
but they can read your heart.

546
00:42:57,360 --> 00:42:59,160
We've all seen plenty of I-persons.

547
00:42:59,160 --> 00:43:00,960
They don't speak or make a sound.

548
00:43:00,960 --> 00:43:02,320
So our Joy Bells

549
00:43:02,320 --> 00:43:05,720
just needs to create a good social environment for them.

550
00:43:05,720 --> 00:43:08,400
Do you think it's the eighties?

551
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,560
It's so tacky.

552
00:43:12,680 --> 00:43:13,480
Wumei.

553
00:43:14,520 --> 00:43:16,440
You son of a bitch, you workplace slacker.

554
00:43:16,440 --> 00:43:18,160
All talk and no action.

555
00:43:18,160 --> 00:43:20,560
Who's older?

556
00:43:20,560 --> 00:43:22,120
Even though I'm older than you,

557
00:43:22,240 --> 00:43:24,720
my heart is still young.

558
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:27,680
If you don't want to be an old slacker,

559
00:43:27,680 --> 00:43:30,120
then get your ass out of the frying pan!

560
00:43:30,120 --> 00:43:31,840
Work with me. Do you dare?

561
00:43:31,840 --> 00:43:33,280
Fine, I will.

562
00:43:33,280 --> 00:43:34,800
You think I'm scared of you?

563
00:43:37,120 --> 00:43:38,440
What are you doing?

564
00:43:38,440 --> 00:43:39,640
Looking all down in the dumps.

565
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:43,920
Your fingernails look pretty nice today.

566
00:43:44,120 --> 00:43:46,640
Press-on nails. You wouldn't get it, bumpkin.

567
00:43:48,680 --> 00:43:49,280
Here, they're yours.

568
00:43:50,280 --> 00:43:51,280
For me?

569
00:43:51,600 --> 00:43:53,440
This set is too small for me to wear anyway.

570
00:43:57,600 --> 00:43:59,000
This event of ours,

571
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:02,000
if it fails, the company will go bankrupt.

572
00:44:02,160 --> 00:44:04,440
Then I'll just have to go to Chengdu to work.

573
00:44:06,920 --> 00:44:08,520
If you go to Chengdu,

574
00:44:08,800 --> 00:44:10,960
Young Boss Zhou will definitely miss you.

575
00:44:19,400 --> 00:44:21,840
I know you all might be a little nervous.

576
00:44:22,920 --> 00:44:24,160
But don't worry.

577
00:44:24,320 --> 00:44:24,960
Here,

578
00:44:25,440 --> 00:44:28,120
you can take off your usual social masks,

579
00:44:28,120 --> 00:44:30,960
and connect with each other sincerely.

580
00:44:31,200 --> 00:44:33,040
Let's get started.

581
00:44:36,880 --> 00:44:38,000
Then tonight,

582
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:40,200
can I invite you to dinner?

583
00:44:40,200 --> 00:44:41,160
Sure.

584
00:44:42,320 --> 00:44:43,120
Is that okay?

585
00:44:45,760 --> 00:44:46,600
I gotta say,

586
00:44:47,560 --> 00:44:49,080
this actually works pretty well.

587
00:44:49,200 --> 00:44:49,760
Right?

588
00:44:49,760 --> 00:44:50,360
Let's take a picture together.

589
00:44:50,360 --> 00:44:50,800
Sure!

590
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:52,000
I'll take it.

591
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:54,200
I feel like I've known you forever.

592
00:44:54,680 --> 00:44:55,880
We're going to be together forever.

593
00:44:56,080 --> 00:44:57,280
E-person Special

594
00:44:58,880 --> 00:45:01,240
The E-person Special is a hunting ground for love.

595
00:45:01,240 --> 00:45:04,240
Reveal your true feelings amidst adventure and thrills.

596
00:45:04,360 --> 00:45:05,600
You've all seen an E-person, right?

597
00:45:05,600 --> 00:45:07,240
They just love to chat.

598
00:45:07,240 --> 00:45:08,440
And love to socialize.

599
00:45:08,640 --> 00:45:09,720
We just need to provide them

600
00:45:09,720 --> 00:45:12,520
with a special environment,

601
00:45:12,520 --> 00:45:15,640
boost their enthusiasm and sense of responsibility,

602
00:45:15,640 --> 00:45:16,680
get them excited,

603
00:45:17,440 --> 00:45:19,640
and the little sparks of love will ignite.

604
00:45:20,720 --> 00:45:21,520
Hey.

605
00:45:22,160 --> 00:45:23,440
Escape Room.

606
00:45:23,880 --> 00:45:24,800
Murder mystery game.

607
00:45:25,400 --> 00:45:26,840
None of the above!

608
00:45:27,400 --> 00:45:29,680
My dear E-person friends,

609
00:45:29,680 --> 00:45:32,880
this is your hunting ground for love.

610
00:45:33,160 --> 00:45:36,560
Here, you'll find not only the challenge of solving puzzles,

611
00:45:36,560 --> 00:45:39,160
but also the thrill of hearts connecting.

612
00:46:00,040 --> 00:46:02,480
Are you sure what's burning is a spark of love?

613
00:46:02,640 --> 00:46:04,000
Don't let it turn out to be just flying sparks.

614
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:05,880
It wouldn't be good if they fly everywhere and burn someone.

615
00:46:05,880 --> 00:46:07,680
What is love, anyway?

616
00:46:07,680 --> 00:46:09,160
If you're scared of every little thing,

617
00:46:09,160 --> 00:46:10,240
then that's not love.

618
00:46:12,680 --> 00:46:15,480
Love is just like instant noodles.

619
00:46:16,360 --> 00:46:18,720
Too fast, and they're undercooked.

620
00:46:18,720 --> 00:46:21,560
Too slow, and they turn to mush.

621
00:46:21,560 --> 00:46:23,480
They have to soak for just the right amount of time.

622
00:46:23,480 --> 00:46:25,680
When they burn your mouth just a little bit,

623
00:46:25,680 --> 00:46:27,720
that's when they're perfect.

624
00:46:28,400 --> 00:46:29,360
Simply put,

625
00:46:29,480 --> 00:46:32,520
young love is a burning passion.

626
00:46:32,520 --> 00:46:34,960
Let it burn when it should!

627
00:46:40,560 --> 00:46:41,560
Thanks, boss!

628
00:46:42,560 --> 00:46:43,600
Success!

629
00:47:00,880 --> 00:47:03,640
I... These shoes are made in Italy.

630
00:47:03,640 --> 00:47:05,920
That stomp just cost you half a year's salary.

631
00:47:05,920 --> 00:47:07,000
You hear me?

632
00:47:07,000 --> 00:47:07,720
I'm really sorry.

633
00:47:07,720 --> 00:47:08,600
I didn't see you.

634
00:47:08,600 --> 00:47:09,400
I'm sorry.

635
00:47:09,400 --> 00:47:11,320
Are you brain-dead?

636
00:47:11,320 --> 00:47:13,240
So clumsy.

637
00:47:24,400 --> 00:47:25,840
Home Funeral Paradise

638
00:47:27,400 --> 00:47:28,680
What a crappy name.

639
00:47:42,920 --> 00:47:44,320
Seriously,

640
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:45,800
you don't even have a waiter here?

641
00:47:47,640 --> 00:47:48,960
Sir.

642
00:47:48,960 --> 00:47:50,120
This isn't a restaurant.

643
00:47:50,120 --> 00:47:51,120
Why would we have waiters?

644
00:47:52,360 --> 00:47:53,160
Sorry about that.

645
00:47:53,160 --> 00:47:53,840
Xiaofang.

646
00:47:55,000 --> 00:47:55,880
I'm so sorry.

647
00:47:56,280 --> 00:47:57,880
What kind of services are you looking for, sir?

648
00:47:57,880 --> 00:48:00,440
Little punk, are you a waiter?
